One thing can behave in many forms. Person can behave differently as:
student
daughter
friend
Same person → many forms.

That is polymorphism.


class Employee {

    void work() {

        System.out.println("This is my work");
    }
}

class Manager extends Employee {

    @Override
    void work() {

        System.out.println("My work");
    }
}

public class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Employee e1 = new Manager();

        e1.work();
    }
}
